────────────────────────────────────────── The Deliberation Engine ───────────────────────────────────────────
Input Feature Request: The CRM should alert us when our relationship with a country goes cold.

╭───────────────────────────────────── Round 1 · PROPOSER (Conf: 0.62) ──────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Proposed Scope (In): ["Nightly job computes last_engagement_date per Country as the most recent existing   │
│ Engagement record linked to any Contact, Mission, or Project of that country. This is derived on the fly   │
│ with no new entity or manual field. ['A1', 'A2']", "A country is flagged 'cold' when days since            │
│ last_engagement_date exceeds a single global threshold, default 90 days, set as one system config value    │
│ and not per country. Countries with no Engagement history are flagged once at go-live with a 'no recorded  │
│ engagement' label. ['A1', 'A2']", "On transition to cold, the system creates one in-app notification for   │
│ the Regional Coordinator(s) already assigned to the country. It includes the last engagement date, the     │
│ last contact engaged, and a link to the Country record. ['A3', 'A4']", "Weekly email digest to each        │
│ Regional Coordinator listing their currently cold countries, with the same fields as the notification.     │
│ Re-reminder at most every 30 days while a country stays cold. ['A3', 'A4']", "Alert auto-clears when a new │
│ Engagement is logged for the country. No acknowledge, snooze, or dismiss action is required of the         │
│ coordinator. ['A1', 'A2']", "Notification and digest visibility inherits the existing Country/Mission      │
│ access model, so users only see alerts for countries they can already see. ['A3']"]                        │
│ Assumptions: ["A1: 'Cold' means no logged Engagement of any type with any contact, mission, or project of  │
│ the country within a single global threshold of 90 days.", 'A2: Engagement records already in the CRM are  │
│ logged as part of normal work and are complete enough to act as the activity signal; Regional Coordinators │
│ will not be asked to enter anything extra.', 'A3: Each country already has an assigned Regional            │
│ Coordinator in the existing access model, and alerts go to that person and respect existing                │
│ Country/Mission permissions.', 'A4: In-app notification plus a weekly email digest is sufficient           │
│ timeliness; real-time alerting is not needed because relationships go cold over weeks, not hours.']        │
